# No `@OnlyIn` (NeoForge 26.1)

Do **not** add `@OnlyIn`, `@OnlyIns`, or `import net.neoforged.api.distmarker.OnlyIn` anywhere in this mod.

NeoForge 26.1 no longer strips `@OnlyIn` members at runtime. Any use triggers a load warning:

> The mod realismsurvival uses the @OnlyIn annotation; the runtime member-stripping behaviour of this annotation is no longer present…

## Instead

- Put client-only code under `com.example.realismsurvival.client`
- Register / reference it only from `RealismSurvivalClient` (`@Mod(..., dist = Dist.CLIENT)`) or `@EventBusSubscriber(..., value = Dist.CLIENT)`
- Do not copy `@OnlyIn` from vanilla sources (e.g. `ClientTooltipComponent`, `ClientBundleTooltip`)

See `REALISM_SURVIVAL_SPEC.md` §10.1.
